 "text": "The Nike swoosh cost $35. 1971, Portland, Oregon. Phil Knight is teaching accounting at Portland State University. His shoe company needs a logo, fast. He hires a graphic design student, Carolyn Davidson. She sketches idea after idea. One looks like motion, a simple curved stroke. Knight's reaction? I don't love it, but maybe it will grow on me. She sends him a bill for $35. The swoosh goes on the shoes. The company becomes Nike, one of the biggest sports brands on Earth. In 1983, Knight surprises her with a gold swoosh ring with a diamond and shares of Nike stock. A $35 sketch, now one of the most famous logos ever. Every legend has a beginning.",
